From c2575b2b017bbd3928dc567b69bdda2104bf8688 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Federico Liva <346224+f-liva@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 26 Nov 2026 15:23:42 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] fix(runtime): keep non-durable offline-queue entries unsent;
 injectable queue storage

An entry pushed to the in-memory offline queue was sendable before
storage.save resolved. A crash between send and save lost the entry
locally while the server had applied it, and a failed save could resend
a mutation that was never durable.

The queue now exposes only the prefix before the first non-durable entry
to the send path. A resolved save releases every id it persisted, not
just the one that triggered it. Queue storage is injectable through the
runtime context so the behaviour is testable.

Refs #155
